AHS-008 — Cognitive Pipeline

Document ID: AHS-008
Title: Cognitive Pipeline
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

Architectural Views: Process, Information

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical cognitive pipeline of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The cognitive pipeline specifies the ordered sequence of engineering cognitive activities through which engineering reality is transformed into explainable decision support.

It provides the normative execution model governing all engineering cognition performed by Atlas.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Pipeline stages
Stage responsibilities
Stage inputs and outputs
Pipeline execution rules
Pipeline control points
Feedback mechanisms

It does not define internal algorithms or implementation technologies.

3. Canonical Definition

The Atlas Cognitive Pipeline is the ordered sequence of cognitive stages that transform engineering observations into explainable engineering decision support while preserving context, evidence, traceability, and engineering intent.

4. Pipeline Objectives

The cognitive pipeline SHALL:

Preserve engineering evidence.
Maintain end-to-end traceability.
Support explainable reasoning.
Ensure deterministic stage responsibilities.
Prevent information loss between stages.
Support feedback-driven refinement.
