Every Atlas implementation SHALL preserve this logical progression, even if stages are distributed or executed asynchronously.

6. Pipeline Stages
Stage 1 — Observation
Purpose

Acquire engineering information from Engineering Reality.

Input

Engineering Reality

Output

Engineering Observation

Stage 2 — Evidence Validation
Purpose

Validate, normalize, and structure observations into Engineering Evidence.

Input

Engineering Observation

Output

Engineering Evidence

Stage 3 — Understanding
Purpose

Interpret validated evidence to construct Engineering Understanding.

Input

Engineering Evidence

Output

Engineering Understanding

Stage 4 — Memory
Purpose

Persist Engineering Understanding together with supporting context, evidence, and provenance.

Input

Engineering Understanding

Output

Engineering Memory

Stage 5 — Knowledge
Purpose

Generalize validated memory into reusable Engineering Knowledge.

Input

Engineering Memory

Output

Engineering Knowledge

Stage 6 — Reasoning
Purpose

Analyze Engineering Understanding and Engineering Knowledge to derive Engineering Conclusions.

Input
Engineering Understanding
Engineering Knowledge
Engineering Context
Engineering Constraints
Output

Engineering Conclusions

Stage 7 — Capability
Purpose

Apply Engineering Conclusions to execute reusable engineering functions.

Input

Engineering Conclusions

Output

Engineering Recommendations and Engineering Outputs

Stage 8 — Decision Support
Purpose

Present explainable recommendations, alternatives, confidence, and rationale for human decision-making.

Input

Engineering Recommendations

Output

Decision Support Artifacts

7. Pipeline Control

The pipeline SHALL support:

Sequential execution
Conditional branching
Parallel execution where semantically valid
Iterative refinement
Human review checkpoints

Control mechanisms SHALL preserve the logical ordering of cognitive responsibilities.

8. Feedback Loops

Engineering cognition is iterative.

Atlas SHALL support feedback from later stages to earlier stages when new information or validation requires refinement.

Reasoning ───────────────┐
                         │
                         ▼
Understanding

Decision Support ────────┐
                         │
                         ▼
Observation

Knowledge ───────────────┐
                         │
                         ▼
Understanding

Feedback SHALL update cognition without violating traceability.

9. Pipeline Invariants

Throughout execution, the following SHALL remain true:

Context SHALL accompany every engineering artifact.
Intent SHALL remain available to every stage.
Constraints SHALL be enforced.
Traceability SHALL be preserved.
Explainability SHALL be maintained.
Confidence SHALL be updated as cognition evolves.

These invariants are mandatory for all pipeline executions.

10. Failure Handling

If a stage cannot produce a valid output, Atlas SHALL:

Record the failure.
Preserve traceability.
Report the failure to upstream consumers.
Prevent invalid artifacts from progressing.
Support recovery or re-execution where appropriate.
11. Conformance

An implementation conforms if it:

Implements all canonical pipeline stages.
Preserves stage responsibilities.
Maintains end-to-end traceability.
Supports required feedback mechanisms.
Preserves pipeline invariants.
12. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Additional specialized stages.
Domain-specific sub-pipelines.
Distributed cognitive pipelines.
Multi-agent execution pipelines.

Such extensions SHALL preserve the canonical cognitive progression defined by this specification.